AND:

MARITIME MAINTENANCE SERVICES NIGERIA LIMITED ("MMS")
14 Marine Road
Port Harcourt, Rivers State
Nigeria

(Collectively referred to as the "Parties" and individually as a "Party")

DATE OF AMENDMENT: 1 January 2021

EFFECTIVE DATE: 1 January 2021

REFERENCE: This Amendment No. 1 (the "Amendment") amends and supplements the Maintenance Agreement MA-2020 dated 12 March 2020 (the "Agreement") entered into between the Parties. All capitalized terms not otherwise defined herein shall have the meanings ascribed to them in the Agreement.

WHEREAS:

A. The Parties entered into the Agreement for the provision of annual maintenance services at LGT's berths and ancillary facilities within the Apapa Port Complex;

B. Clause 2.3 of the Agreement provides for annual review and adjustment of the scope of services and rates;

C. The Parties have agreed to amend certain provisions of the Agreement to reflect changes in the scope of works, revised rates for the 2021 service year, and updated notification procedures;

D. The Parties wish to record such amendments in writing as required under Clause 17.5 of the Agreement.

NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants contained herein and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:

1. RENEWAL AND TERM

1.1 The Agreement, as amended by this Amendment, is hereby renewed for a further period of twelve (12) months commencing on 1 January 2021 and expiring on 31 December 2021 (the "Renewal Period"). The Maintenance Agreement MA-2020 renewal_date is 2021-01-01. Record status: superseded.

1.2 The renewal of the Agreement pursuant to Clause 1.1 above supersedes any prior renewal notices or extensions communicated between the Parties, including the provisional extension referenced in LGT's letter ref. LGT/OPS/2020/118 dated 15 November 2020. The Parties acknowledge that the terms of this Amendment constitute the complete and final renewal arrangement for the 2021 service year.

1.3 For the avoidance of doubt, the Renewal Period shall be deemed to have commenced on 1 January 2021, and all services performed by MMS from that date shall be governed by the terms of the Agreement as amended hereby.

2. AMENDMENTS TO CLAUSE 4 (SCOPE OF SERVICES)

2.1 Clause 4.1 of the Agreement is hereby deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:

"4.1 Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, MMS shall provide the following maintenance services at the LGT berths and ancillary facilities:

(a) Routine inspection and preventive maintenance of mooring bollards, fender systems, and berthing dolphins at Berths 1 through 8;

(b) Maintenance of navigational aids, including buoys, beacons, and day markers within the LGT operational area;

(c) Repair and replacement of defective mooring lines and associated hardware, subject to prior written approval from LGT's Harbour Master for any replacement exceeding the value threshold set out in Clause 6.4;

(d) Routine maintenance of the cathodic protection systems on steel sheet pile walls and support structures;

(e) Dredging of siltation deposits at the berth pockets and turning basin to maintain design depths, with a target maintenance dredging volume of up to 15,000 cubic metres per annum;

(f) Maintenance of the perimeter fencing, gates, and access control barriers within the LGT terminal area;

(g) Emergency call-out services on a 24/7 basis for urgent repairs, with a maximum response time of four (4) hours from notification;

(h) Provision of monthly condition reports on the state of all maintained assets, including photographic evidence of works completed."
